# Plan removal and Clear controls

Add destructive controls for removing the final custom-plan step and resetting either plan type.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The final step in a construction plan has a bin icon.
- [x] Tapping the bin removes only that final step; earlier ordered steps remain unchanged.
- [x] A Cards plan has a Clear button that removes every selected card.
- [x] A Constructions plan has a Clear button that removes every construction step.
- [x] Clear is disabled or has no destructive effect when the plan content is already empty.
- [x] Clear and bin operations affect only the editor draft until Save is selected.
- [x] Cancel restores the previously saved plan contents after any removal or Clear action.
- [x] Destructive controls have accessible labels and app/test bundles compile.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- Construction-step reordering and arbitrary middle-step deletion are not requested.
- The final-step restriction preserves the validity assumptions of later ordered steps.

## Verification

- Add domain/editor coverage for final-step removal, clearing both plan types, Cancel, and Save.

## Evidence

- Added `CustomPlan` mutations for kind-specific clearing and final-step removal, with focused unit coverage.
- Added accessible Clear buttons to both editors and a trash action rendered only on the final construction row.
- Extended UI coverage for Cards Clear and final construction-step removal/disabled empty Clear.
